# Prettier reads the repository-root .gitignore but not nested ones, so
# cli/.gitignore does not keep the compiled CLI out of `npm run format:check`.
#
# That matters because .husky/pre-commit runs both `format:check` and
# `npm run secureflow`: the latter needs cli/dist to exist, the former failed on
# it. Anyone who has installed the CLI's dependencies has cli/dist, because
# cli/package.json builds it from its `prepare` script — so the hook could not
# pass at all.
cli/dist/

# Generated output and reports. The root .gitignore already keeps these out of
# git; list them here so a build in a nested workspace cannot break the hook the
# same way.
**/.next/
**/out/
**/build/
**/coverage/
**/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
helm/
